  "body": "Firefox requires a secure context to call `registerProtocolHandler`. Chrome would like to require a secure context to call `registerProtocolHandler` and `unregisterProtocolHandler`. \r\n\r\nAs protocol handlers are a \"Powerful Capability\" (changing the configuration and behavior of the user agent), it makes sense to require that they be installed from secure contexts.\r\n\r\nFiling in advance of sending an I2D for Chromium. \r\nhttps://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/1892213\r\n",
